## Type rules

| Role | Size (desktop → mobile) | Weight | Tracking | Line height |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Display / h1 | 80 → 42px | 700 (Outfit 500) | −0.042em (Jakarta −0.035, Outfit −0.028) | 1.0 |
| Section h2 | 54 → 32px | same | slightly looser than h1 | 1.05 |
| Feature h3 | 38 → 24px | same | | 1.1 |
| Card title `.t-title` | 16–17px | 600 | −0.015em | 1.35 |
| Lead | 21 → 17.5px | 400 | −0.011em | 1.5, ink-3 |
| Body | 16.5px | 400 | 0 | 1.6 |
| Small / micro | 14.5 / 13px | 400–550 | 0 | 1.5 |
| Eyebrow | 12px uppercase | 600 | +0.11em | ink-3 |
| Buttons | 15px (sm 13.5) | 600 | −0.01em | — |

- Headlines are short claims in sentence case that end with a period. Two lines is ideal, three is the max.
- One signature device per headline, never several: **muted second phrase** (`<span class="t-muted">`, display sizes only), **marker highlight** on 1–3 words (`<span class="hl">`; add `t-accent` only with the cobalt accent — blue on lime), or **serif italic word** (`<em class="t-serif">`).
- Prices, versions, shortcuts and counters use mono (`.t-mono`, `<kbd>`).
- `--ink-4` and `.t-muted` are only for text ≥24px (they pass AA for large text only). Anything smaller uses ink-3 or darker.
- Floor: 13px for real page copy; 12px for eyebrows, badge tags and keycaps. Text inside decorative product mockups may go down to 10px — mark non-interactive mockups `aria-hidden="true"`.

## Spacing & shape

- 4px base: 4 8 12 16 20 24 32 40 48 64 80 112 128. Sections use `--section-y`; feature blocks inside a section are separated by `.stack`.
- Container 1120px; centered text blocks max 620–680px; splits are 1fr / 1.1fr.
- Radii: 7 (kbd) · 10 · 14 (inputs, inner tiles, windows) · 20 (cards) · 28 (panels, stages, bentos) · 32 (big carded-variant cards) · pill (every button, chip, badge, nav). Nested radius = outer − padding, never below 8px.
- Depth = hairline ring + soft long shadow. Never a single dark short shadow; never a border and a shadow on the same edge.
- Rhythm: `.section--alt` is a hairline-divided white band in `white`, a soft gray band in `mist`; in carded and cream, keep one canvas and let cards carry contrast.
- Hero visual overlap: add `.bleed` to `.hero__visual` and `.after-bleed` to the next section (a `.section--alt`).

## Page anatomy (canonical order)

1. **Nav** — floating glass pill: app icon + name · 3–5 anchor links · small primary CTA (`btn-sm`, may carry the price in a `.tag`).
2. **Hero** — badge (`New` tag + real release note, or dot + real stat) → h1 → lead (1–3 lines) → CTA row (primary + secondary) → `.trust` microline (price model · refund · OS requirement) → product visual in a `.stage`. Use `.hero--split` when the visual is interactive and tall.
3. **Proof strip** — real logos (grayscale, 55% opacity) or a real count. Skip if none.
4. **Problem → solution** — two `.card--flat`: the old way, and this app as `.card--chosen`, each with a small visual.
5. **Feature deep-dives** — 2–4 `.split` blocks (alternate with `.split--flip`): eyebrow with icon → h3 → `.t-small` or `.lead` → chips of sub-features → visual on a `.stage--soft`.
6. **Everything else** — `.grid-3` of `.tile`s with `.icon-tile` icons.
7. **Try it here** (signature move) — `.try` layout: a `.card` of controls (segmented, chips, `.range`, `.switch`) beside a live preview on a `.stage`. Make the visitor touch the product with real JavaScript.
8. **Social proof** — real posts only. 1–2 quotes → `.quote--feature`; 3+ → `.quotes` masonry. Use the person's photo only if supplied, otherwise `.avatar` initials.
9. **Pricing** — one `.price-card`: head with app icon, name and requirements; price (struck anchor only if the regular price is real); checklist; full-width CTA; refund line.
10. **FAQ** — `<details>` list, 5–8 honest questions.
11. **Final CTA** — 88px app icon with `--shadow-2`, h2 with muted second phrase, CTA row.
12. **Footer** — one quiet row: icon + name, links, "Made by …".

## CTAs by distribution

- **Direct sale**: "Buy — $X" (candy or ink) + secondary "Try it on this page" / "Try free for 7 days".
- **App Store**: ink pill with the Apple logo, "Download on the App Store", or Apple's official badge artwork; price goes in the trust line.
- **Free / freemium**: "Download for Mac", "Get started free".
- **Not launched**: `.join` email field + "Join the waitlist", and a "Coming soon" badge. Never link to a store page that doesn't exist.

## Product visuals

- Build the app's UI in HTML: real labels, plausible data, the product's own colors (define them as extra custom properties, e.g. `--app-bg`). Dark app UI on a bold wallpaper is the strongest hero combo.
- Frames: `.window` (titled app window) · `.desktop` + `.menubar` + `.popover` (menu-bar apps) · `.phone` with `.phone__status` and `.phone__body` (iOS). Bold `--wallpaper` for the hero stage, `.stage--soft` for every other stage.
- Up to three `.float` fragments (notification, chat bubble, widget) around the hero frame; they hide under 760px, so lay out their insides with an inner wrapper and never override `.float`'s `display`.
- Icons: inline SVGs drawn in Lucide's style (24px grid, 1.75 stroke, round caps), sized 18–20px, so files stay self-contained. If you load an icon CDN, pin an exact version. No emoji as icons.
- Photos: no stock photography. Real photos the user supplies are fine in a 28–32px-radius frame, one per page at most.

## Motion

- `--ease-out` for things moving into place; `--ease-spring` only for press and toggle feedback.
- Press 120ms · hover 200ms · UI state 300ms · reveal 700ms with 80ms stagger.
- Hover lifts 1–2px and deepens the shadow; press scales to 0.97. No looping bounces, parallax or scroll-jacking. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Copy voice

- Plain, specific, confident. Say what it does, then what that gets you. Short sentences, periods.
- Headline shapes (write new words every time): "[Outcome], without [pain]." · "[Verb] once. [Result]." · "The [category] for [platform]." · "[Short claim]. [Muted payoff]."
- CTAs name the action, and the price when it's a purchase.
- Microcopy removes risk: one-time purchase, refund window, OS requirement, "No account needed".
- Banned: revolutionize, supercharge, seamless, unlock, next-level, game-changer, leverage, empower, exclamation marks, emoji in headings.

## Light, dark, responsive

- Always light. Don't follow `prefers-color-scheme` and don't add a dark mode unless the user explicitly asks. If they do, set `data-theme="dark"` (every mood has dark tokens), or mirror the dark blocks under `@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark)` as the comment in the foundation says. Components never get theme-specific rules — only tokens change.
- Breakpoints: 900px (grids → 2 col, splits and split hero stack) and 640px (1 col, 18px gutter, trust line stacks). Under 760px the nav keeps icon, name and CTA.
- At 375px: no horizontal scroll, h1 42–48px, CTA rows wrap, stage content scales or crops, touch targets ≥44px on coarse pointers.

## Web app UI (not marketing)

Same tokens, denser: body 14px, controls 32–36px, radii 10–14px, cards with `--ring`, ink primary buttons, segmented controls for views, chips for filters, `kbd` hints beside actions. Accent only for the primary action and selection states.

## Pre-ship checklist

- [ ] One mood, one accent; the accent only fills its three roles.
- [ ] Headlines: sentence case, end with a period, ≤3 lines, negative tracking, one signature device max.
- [ ] Every button is a pill; primary vs secondary is obvious; the hero has a trust line.
- [ ] Product visuals are real UI in frames, not gray boxes or stock images.
- [ ] Colors, radii and shadows come from tokens; fixed colors only in device chrome (traffic lights, bezels, keycaps, menu bars).
- [ ] Body text never wider than 680px; centered paragraphs ≤620px.
- [ ] No invented numbers, reviews, logos, press or store links. Placeholders are visibly marked.
- [ ] Checked at 1440px and 375px; no horizontal scroll.
- [ ] Small text ≥ ink-3 contrast; visible focus rings; reduced motion respected; images have alt text; decorative mockups are `aria-hidden`.

## Anti-patterns (instant tells of a generic AI page)

Purple-to-pink gradient blobs · glassmorphism on every card · neon glows · three emoji feature cards · default Inter at zero tracking · Title Case Headlines · gray placeholder rectangles · stock photos · 1px `#ddd` borders with heavy gray shadows · more than one accent · centered walls of text · fake "10,000+ happy users" · buzzword copy.

